---
import { CRITICISM_EMAIL } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const email = CRITICISM_EMAIL.trim();
const mailto = `mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Criticism — Compost et Coagula')}`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Criticism" description="An invitation to question the arguments, challenge the readings, and correct the errors in Compost et Coagula.">
	<article class="criticism">
		<header class="page-header">
			<h1>Criticism</h1>
			<p class="lede">These essays are open to disagreement.</p>
		</header>
		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				I welcome criticism of the writing here: an error in a source, a reading that does not hold up,
				a conclusion the evidence cannot carry, or a question the essay has failed to ask.
				You do not need to share my commitments or offer a finished counterargument to point out a problem.
			</p>
			<p>
				This work crosses theology, environmental science, and history. Those crossings need scrutiny.
				Where does an analogy clarify something, and where does it obscure the particular people, places,
				or processes under discussion? What have I mistaken, simplified, or left out?
			</p>

			<h2>Writing to me</h2>
			<p>
				Please name the essay and, where possible, quote or link to the passage you are responding to.
				Tell me what you think is wrong and why. A source or page reference is helpful when the disagreement
				turns on evidence; a brief objection is welcome too.
			</p>
			{email ? (
				<p><a href={mailto}>Email your criticism</a> · <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></p>
			) : (
				<p>A dedicated email address for this correspondence will be added here soon.</p>
			)}

			<h2>Corrections and reconsiderations</h2>
			<p>
				Factual errors deserve explicit correction. Changes that matter to an essay’s argument are recorded
				on its page. Later notes can add evidence, mark an unresolved question, or reconsider a reading,
				so that the development of the work remains visible. Small typographical fixes may be made silently.
			</p>
			<p>
				Disagreement may also remain disagreement. I cannot promise a reply to every message, but criticism
				does not have to persuade me immediately to be worth sending.
			</p>

			<h2>Correspondence</h2>
			<p>
				Writing to me is not permission to publish your message. I will ask before quoting private
				correspondence or identifying its author in an acknowledgment.
			</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.criticism {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-inline: auto;
	}
</style>
